BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Film & Media Studies Colloquium with Technical Director Warren Coc
 kerham
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261110T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261110T140000
DTSTAMP:20261109T212104Z
UID:dartmouth-83203@free-food-dartmouth
SEQUENCE:0
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:Original event page(s):\nhttps://home.dartmouth.edu/events/eve
 nt?event=83203\n\nDescription:\nJoin the Department of Film & Media Studie
 s for our fall colloquium with Technical Director\, Warren Cockerham.\nRed
 actions/Reductions: A Reopening\nCollections upon collections. Images\, so
 unds\, documents\, family histories\, and fragments of experiences that re
 sist resolution. Occasionally something emerges from the accumulation. A f
 ilm\, and attempt to make sense of something\, or perhaps to make it more 
 mysterious. These works are not finished histories\, but pieces of an open
  archive subject to revision\, reconsideration\, and play. Returning to a 
 selection of earlier films\, some rarely shown\, I am reopening this archi
 ve not simply to revisit what has been made\, but to add to it\, to make n
 ew experiences from old materials\, and to see what else might emerge as t
 he past continues to shockingly unfold in the present.\nWarren Cockerham\n
 is a filmmaker\, educater\, and cinema technologist. He recevied his MFA f
 rom the School of the Art Institute of Chicago in 2010. His early work in 
 media access and advocacy led to the founding of FilmLAB@1512\, a film and
  video program for teenagers in Chicago's North Lawndale community.\nHis f
 ilm work is driven by an interest in power structures within familial and 
 intimate relationships\, and how those dynamics are shaped\, obscured\, or
  reframed through archival media–both public and private. His projects t
 end to resist conventional narrative\, instead organizing themselves aroun
 d a set of problems or tensions. His work has screened at venues across th
 e U.S. and internationally.\n\nSponsor / organizer: Film & Media Studies D
 epartment\n\nAudience: Public\n\nSource: Dartmouth\n\nWhy this was include
 d: Free Food category\n\nFood availability is inferred from the source lis
 ting\; verify details before attending.
LAST-MODIFIED:20261109T212104Z
LOCATION:Loew Auditorium\, Black Family Visual Arts Center
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://home.dartmouth.edu/events/event?event=83203
X-MICROSOFT-CDO-BUSYSTATUS:FREE
END:VEVENT
